  "public_messages": [
    "I’ll inspect the project instructions and the OpenSocrates controller first, then build the app and verify the requested workflows against the running local service.",
    "The project is an empty starter, so I’m using Python’s standard library and SQLite to keep startup local and reproducible. SQLite write transactions will serialize reservations and idempotency checks; tenant scoping and role checks will sit at the API boundary and in every data query.",
    "The core service and interface are in place. I’m adding integration checks around the HTTP boundary, including a competing reservation race and a real process restart, plus a benchmark that starts an isolated seeded instance so its results can be reproduced without affecting a user’s data.",
    "The API tests now pass, including concurrent reservations and restart replay. The isolated 8-client run completed 600 reads and 100 order-creation writes with zero errors; I’m moving on to the real browser workflow and will keep the recorded numbers tied to that exact command and environment.",
    "The first browser run exposed an automation selector ambiguity: the status text appears in both the header badge and metadata. I narrowed the check to the header badge; the next run is exercising the same user flow with short, named checkpoints so any actual UI issue is easy to localize.",
    "The final expanded HTTP suite passes, including identical concurrent reserve replay and a cross-tenant cursor check; JavaScript syntax and the no-dependency setup check also pass. I’m restarting the browser instance on the final backend now, then I’ll finalize the verification record and inspect the workspace for generated artifacts or missed requirements.",
    "Built DepotFlow with a Python standard-library API, SQLite persistence, and a responsive workflow UI. Start it with:\n\n```sh\n./setup.sh\nSEED_DEMO=1 DATA_DIR=\"$PWD/data\" PORT=8000 ./run.sh\n```\n\nThe integration suite passed all 8 tests, including tenant isolation, concurrent reservations, retries, returns, and restart persistence. The browser workflow passed at desktop and 390px width with no page errors. The benchmark completed 600 reads and 100 writes with zero errors: 1,742.75 reads/s and 290.46 writes/s in the mixed run.\n\nSee [README.md](<CELL>/workspace/README.md), [architecture.md](<CELL>/workspace/architecture.md), and the [verification record](<CELL>/workspace/evidence/verification.md). The browser screenshot and raw benchmark results are in `evidence/`. The benchmark is a short local workload; SQLite serializes writes, so it does not establish production capacity.\n\nOpenSocrates native activation is unconfirmed; I read the installed canonical reference in full.\n\nOpenSocrates grounding: trade-off-analysis@3"
